### 2. The Controller

**File:** `com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.Controller.LhoTransferController.java`

This controller exposes the endpoints for the UI. It returns your standard `ApiResponse` format, ensuring the frontend handles the data consistently with other masters.

```java
package com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.Controller;

import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.ApiResponse;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.CommonRequestDto;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.PaginatedResponseDto;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto.SearchRequest;
import com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.service.CommonMasterService;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@Slf4j
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/lho-transfers")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class LhoTransferController {

    private final CommonMasterService service;

    /**
     * POST /api/lho-transfers/search
     * Fetches all LHO Transfer requests with support for dynamic filters, 
     * pagination, and sorting.
     */
    @PostMapping("/search")
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<PaginatedResponseDto<CommonRequestDto>>> searchLhoTransfers(
            @RequestBody SearchRequest request) {
        log.info("Received request to search LHO Transfers");
        PaginatedResponseDto<CommonRequestDto> response = service.searchLhoTransfers(request);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ApiResponse.success(response, "LHO Transfers fetched successfully"));
    }

    /**
     * GET /api/lho-transfers/{id}
     * Fetches details for a specific LHO Transfer.
     */
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<CommonRequestDto>> getLhoTransferById(@PathVariable Long id) {
        log.info("Received request to fetch LHO Transfer ID: {}", id);
        CommonRequestDto response = service.getLhoTransferById(id);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ApiResponse.success(response));
    }
}

```

### How to test this:

To test the search via Postman, send a `POST` request to `/api/lho-transfers/search` with a body like this:

```json
{
    "page": 0,
    "size": 10,
    "sortField": "requestDate",
    "sortOrder": "DESC",
    "filters": [
        {
            "field": "status",
            "operator": "equals",
            "value": "P"
        }
    ]
}

```

This will return all **Pending (P)** requests where the `REQ_TYPE` is `LHO_TRANSFER`.

